[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Italian Game"]
[Variation "Rousseau Gambit, Accepted"]
[ECO "C50"]
[Character "gambit,tactical"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "fork,queen-trap"]
[Themes "pawn-back,central-pawn"]
[For "black"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "4.exf5"]
[Start "1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 f5"]

4. exf5 $6 { Takes the pawn, but it leaves the centre and the engine thinks Black is fine after the reply. } 4... e4 { Kicks the knight with the pawn, opens the queen's diagonal to h4 and gets time. The f5 pawn will be won back. } 5. Nd4 ( 5. Ng5 Qxg5 { The knight has no defender on g5 now that the f-pawn has gone, so the queen takes it for free. } 6. O-O Qxf5 ) ( 5. Ne5 Nxe5 { Takes the knight; the pawn on e5 was just a decoy. } 6. Bb3 Qg5 { Hits g2 and keeps the extra knight. } ) 5... Nf6 { Develops and covers d5, so the knight on d4 and the e4 pawn are both under pressure. } 6. Nxc6 bxc6 { Recaptures towards the centre. The open b-file and a strong d5 are worth more than the doubled pawns. } 7. d4 d5 { Builds a pawn centre, and the bishop on c8 can win the pawn on f5 back. } 8. Bb3 Bxf5 { Takes the pawn back. Black has a solid centre and a lead in development, so the gambit has paid off. } 9. c4 Be7 { Gets ready to castle. Level game: castle, then attack the white centre with ...Rb8 or ...Qd7. } *
